-- Expected (line, col, len, role) for copula.id. HAND-WRITTEN from the law,
-- never read off the projector: the golden per-byte corpus catches regressions,
-- these rows catch being WRONG.
--
-- What this fixture discriminates, and it is the line gaps/GAP-078.md was filed
-- over: THE COPULA/INVOKE SPLIT, AND SPACING IS NOT THE DECIDER. `grammar.md`
-- R1 is — "IS never takes an argument group; INVOKE always does" — and R1 is
-- NORMATIVE (Pass 108). CLAUDE.md §0d's spaced-versus-tight sentence is a
-- canonical-layout COROLLARY: it renders the decision, it does not make it.
--
-- Line 3 separates them. `count:u32` is TIGHT and carries no call group, so R1
-- says copula and spacing says invoke. A scanner that highlights line 3 purple
-- has failed H-1, and `tools/lsp/src/highlight.id` used to be that scanner
-- until GAP-078 ruled. Line 4's `lx:read(` is tight AND grouped, so it is the
-- invoke — the two live in the same file on purpose.
--
-- `total`, `count`, `n`, `lx`, `number` are ordinary bindings and they are
-- `place`: blue, heavy at definition, the role this document used to call
-- `name` and leave UNHUED. An unhued role cannot satisfy H-6's total function,
-- which is why the unhued reading measured 20% coverage and this one measures
-- 100%. -- gap[078]
spans = {
    { 1, 1, 9, "comment" },
    { 2, 1, 5, "place" },
    { 2, 6, 1, "copula" },
    { 2, 8, 3, "descriptor" },
    { 3, 1, 5, "place" },
    { 3, 6, 1, "copula" },
    { 3, 7, 3, "descriptor" },
    { 4, 1, 1, "place" },
